Z||000000||jmw||12-06-2000||04:56 PM||||Can anyone help me out with some pricing info? <P>First question: NTB has discontinued Pirelli Formula GTs (S-rated blackwalls) for $26 each + tax in my size (215/60/14). Supposedly they're comparable to BF Goodrich Radial T/A's ($50 + shipping, but no tax, at tirerack.com) which is what I was after to begin with. [BTW, NTB will match tirerack's prices]. My question is, are these Pirelli's truly comparable or should I stick with the BFGs? <P>Also, they charge $10 ea. to mount & balance, and $2.50 for stems, plus $54.99 for an alignment. Is this a fair price?  If not, what is?<P>Second question: NTB has Monroe shocks for $22.99 ea. + $11 ea. to install. Is that a fair price? If not, what is? <P>Third question: they have struts for $59.99 ea. + $34.99 ea. to install. Is that a fair price? If not, what is?<P>I am determined not to get gypped ever again so any advice y'all can offer would be greatly appreciated.<P>Thanks!<p>[This message has been edited by jmw (edited 12-06-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000001||Fformula88||12-06-2000||06:52 PM||||Tires:  Not sure how comparable that model Perrelli is, but I am sure the BFG's are good tires.  Personally, I like Dunlop D60 A2 JLB'.  <P>Struts/Shocks... sounds like a good deal to me.  Especially the shocks... they are easy to replace but I would have expected that they would have hit you with a larger labor cost than that!||||reg||1
